# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# .gitignore — Files to ignore in version control (Git)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# WHAT IS .gitignore? A list of files/folders that Git should NOT track.
# These are either:
# - Generated files (can be recreated from source)
# - Sensitive files (API keys, passwords)
# - Large files (node_modules, build output)
# - Local-only files (editor settings, OS files)
#
# WHY IGNORE node_modules? It contains ~1000+ packages (50MB+).
# Instead of storing them in Git, we store package.json and run `npm install`
# to recreate the exact same dependencies. This keeps the repo small.
#
# WHY IGNORE dist/? It's the build output — generated from source code.
# You can recreate it by running `npm run build`.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Log files are created by npm/yarn/pnpm when things go wrong
# They're local debugging artifacts, not source code
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

# ── Dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# node_modules contains all installed packages (50MB+)
# Recreated by running: npm install
node_modules

# ── Build Output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# dist/ contains the production build (minified JS/CSS/HTML)
# Recreated by running: npm run build
dist

# dist-ssr/ contains server-side rendering build output
dist-ssr

# ── Local Configuration ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .local files contain machine-specific settings (e.g., API keys for dev)
# Never commit these — they're different on every developer's machine
*.local

# ── Editor Directories and Files ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Each developer has their own editor settings — don't force yours on others

# VS Code (most common)
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json  # But DO track recommended extensions

# JetBrains IDEs (WebStorm, IntelliJ)
.idea

# macOS system files
.DS_Store

# Visual Studio
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln

# Vim/Neovim swap files
*.sw?
